    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-assistant-for-pfas-clear-and-swift-projects": {
      "title": "Student assistant for PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects",
      "description": "Student assistant for PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Environmental Science - Environmental chemistry & toxicology Student assistant for PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects Deadline 20 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Nov Department of Environmental Science - Environmental chemistry & toxicology Frederiksborgvej 399 4000 Roskilde Fixed term part-time position 1 Nov 2026 - 31 Oct 2028 8 hours per week ID: 170639 Apply Are you passionate about environmental chemistry or mass spectrometry and can you contribute to the development of the project PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT? The Department of Environmental Science at Aarhus University is looking for one student assistant. Expected start date and duration of employment The position is from 1 November 2026, or as soon as possible thereafter, and for a period of 2 years. Job description You will be contributing to the organization of project datasets, digitalization and integration of data, and curation of research data and associated metadata. You will support harmonization of datasets, including data structures, variable names, units and metadata, and contribute to basic quality control and documentation. You will assist with data processing, tabulation and visualization when relevant. These activities will be carried out in close collaboration with researchers working in the PFAS-CLEAR and SWIFT projects. Your profile Experience in handling and treating research datasets, environmental data and experimental metadata. Experience with SciexOS is an advantage. Experience with Excel and/or data handling in R or Python is an advantage. Be thorough and able to work independently and disciplined. Be able to communicate in English. Have an interest in environmental chemistry and data integration. The qualification requirement is enrolment at an institution of higher education. Who we are The Department of Environmental Science has about 150 employees working in basic and problem-oriented research within environmental science, including chemical and physical processes and interactions between environment and society. The department also carries out research-based consultancy for the public sector and provides research-based advice. The academic expertise ranges from atmospheric chemistry and physics, via environmental chemistry, microbiology and biotechnology to environmental economics, environmental geography, political science and sociology. The department is located in Roskilde, Denmark. This position will be based in the section for Environmental Chemistry and Toxicology. What we offer The department offers: high-quality research in a strong international network state-of-the-art research infrastructure, laboratories and access to shared equipment possibilities for scientific and personal development and career building an interdisciplinary environment with many national and international collaborators a research group with close working relationships and mutual support a climate encouraging lively, open and critical discussion within and across different fields of research Place of work and area of employment The place of work is Aarhus University, Department of Environmental Science, Frederiksborgvej 399, 4000 Roskilde, Denmark. Please note that the place of work is Roskilde, not Aarhus. Contact information For further information, please contact: Associate Professor Pedro Carvalho, +45 87 15 84 62, [email protected] Deadline Applications must be received no later than 20 October 2026. Formalities and salary range Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Union of Commercial and Clerical Employees in Denmark/State (HK/Stat) for clerical staff, laboratory technicians and IT employees and the joint collective agreement concluded between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Organisations of Public Employees - Denmark - Danish State Sector (the OAO-S joint collective agreement). Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Pedro Carvalho Associate Professor, Head of Section, Department of Environmental Science - Environmental chemistry & toxicology +4587158462 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4522521469 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Tuesday 20 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-assistant-at-the-center-for-hybrid-intelligence-chi-at-department-of-management": {
      "title": "Student Assistant",
      "description": "Student Assistant at the Center for Hybrid Intelligence (CHI) at Department of Management - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Management Student Assistant at the Center for Hybrid Intelligence (CHI) at Department of Management Deadline 21 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Nov Department of Management Universitetsbyen 61 8000 Aarhus C Part-time position 12 hours per week ID: 170810 Apply The AI-first narrative promises speed and automation, but risks eroding human meaning and agency. At the Center for Hybrid Intelligence (CHI), we believe in another path and that is combining human creativity, ethics and judgment with the scalability of AI. We are an interdisciplinary team of researchers and practitioners at the Department of Management, Aarhus BSS, Aarhus University. We develop frameworks and tools for human-AI collaboration, such as FERC and the 4P Framework, do a lot of workshops, exploring digital interfaces and we are behind the Hybrid Intelligence Manifesto, supported by over 900 signatories. Our websites are where all of this meets the world. We are looking for a creative and student assistant where your main task is to help us improve and develop our websites. The main website is made with Wordpress. As our student assistant, you will help shape how researchers, companies and the public experience hybrid intelligence. Our websites are one of the most important ways we share our activities on hybrid intelligence, where humans and AI meet to create meaningful innovation. As part of our team, you will work on live websites with real users and real impact. Your tasks Your tasks will include: Web design & maintenance: Designing, building and improving our websites so they are visually appealing, user-friendly and up to date. This is your main task. Improving structure, navigation and user experience across our sites. Graphic design: Creating visual material and graphics that fit our identity. Content: Publishing and updating content that communicates our projects, results and events to both academic and broader audiences. Ad hoc: We are a fast-moving team with many exciting projects, so you can expect a dynamic work environment with diverse tasks. We expect that you Have skills in web design. Knowledge or/and experience with WordPress Have an eye for aesthetics and UX. Be able to show examples of your work (a portfolio or a project is enough). Work in a structured and independent way. Have an interest in AI and technology Can communicate effectively, both in writing and verbally, in English and Danish. Nice to have: Experience in graphic design and image editing (e.g. Figma, Adobe or similar), Basic HTML/CSS You do not need to know everything above. Curiosity and a good eye for design matter more. What we offer Highly relevant practical experience for aspiring web designers, with your work visible to the public. Close collaboration with both students, professors, partners from different fields so you can grow your network and gain experience in AI. A young, interdisciplinary team that aims to create impact with our research, and a working environment characterised by respect, appreciation and collaboration. Who we are The Department of Management is part of Aarhus BSS , Aarhus University – a top 100 university. Aarhus BSS has achieved the triple-crown AACSB, AMBA and EQUIS accreditations. The department has an international research and teaching environment, employs approximately 160 Danish and international researchers, academic staff, and PhD students. We excel in business management, including strategy, innovation, marketing, organisation, digitalisation, and accounting. Our aim is to deliver high-quality research, with a strong emphasis on publishing in leading academic journals and presenting at recognised conferences. You can read more about the Department of Management at: http://mgmt.au.dk . Contact information For further information about the position, please contact Rigmor Lyck by phone at 2479 6701 or by [email protected] If you need assistance uploading your application or have questions regarding the recruitment process, please contact HR-Coordinator Line Greve Brunhøi at: [email protected] . Practical information The average working time is approximately 12 hours per week, and the place of work is Universitetsbyen 614, 8000 Aarhus C. Applications must be submitted electronically and received no later than 21 October 2026. The expected starting date is 1 November 2026, or as soon as possible thereafter. Please submit a short, motivated application and your CV, including information about your degree programme and current semester. Terms of employment You will be employed as an hourly-paid student assistant under the collective agreement between the Danish Ministry of Finance and the Organisations of Public Employees – Denmark (OAO-S Collective Agreement, State Sector), as well as the organisational agreement for clerical employees, laboratory technicians and IT staff (HK). Aarhus University Aarhus University is an academically diverse and research-intensive university with a strong commitment to high-quality research and education and the development of society nationally and globally. The university offers an inspiring research and teaching environment to its 37,000 students (FTEs) and 8,700 employees and has an annual revenue of EUR 1.106 billion. Learn more at www.international.au.dk/ Questions about the position\n                            ? Jacob Sherson Associate Professor, Department of Management +4528775765 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Aarhus BSS Administrative Centre - Aarhus BSS HR and PhD Administration +4587150584 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Wednesday 21 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/vi-mangler-studentermedhjaelpere-i-de-kirurgiske-forskningslaboratorier-paa-skejby-er-det-noget-for-dig-1": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "Vi mangler studentermedhjælpere i De Kirurgiske Forskningslaboratorier på Skejby – er det noget for dig? - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Clinical Medicine - The Surgical Research Laboratories, SKS Vi mangler studentermedhjælpere i De Kirurgiske Forskningslaboratorier på Skejby – er det noget for dig? Deadline 22 Oct 23:59 CEST Expected start 1 Jan Department of Clinical Medicine - The Surgical Research Laboratories, SKS Palle Juul-Jensens Boulevard 99 8200 Aarhus N Part-time position 1 hours per week ID: 170774 Apply De Kirurgiske Forskningslaboratorier ved Institut for Klinisk Medicin, Aarhus Universitets sundhedsvidenskabelige fakultet, SUND, søger 5-6 studentermedhjælpere til at assistere personalet ved afvikling af kurser, forskning og daglig drift pr. 1. januar 2027 eller snarest muligt derefter. Stillingerne er deltidsstillinger. De enkelte ansættelser er betinget af, at du er studerende, og de ophører, når du dimitterer eller ikke længere er indskrevet på en uddannelse. Institut for Klinisk Medicin Som studentermedhjælper på Institut for Klinisk Medicin bliver du en del af det formentlig største sundhedsvidenskabelige forskningsinstitut i Danmark. Den kliniske forskning dækker alle de lægefaglige specialer og foregår i samspil med universitetshospitalet og regionshospitalerne i Region Midtjylland. Vi råder over ca. 30.000 kvm moderne forskningsfaciliteter til eksperimentel kirurgi og medicin, dyrefaciliteter samt avancerede scannere. Instituttet har det overordnede ansvar for kandidatuddannelserne i medicin og i molekylær medicin. På instituttet er vi ca. 670 videnskabelige medarbejdere, 500 ph.d.-studerende og 160 teknisk/administrative medarbejdere, der samarbejder på tværs af fagområder. Som studenterunderviser vil du komme til at arbejde på Aarhus Universitetshospital eller et andet hospital i Region Midtjylland. Du kan læse mere om instituttet her og om fakultetet her . Dine arbejdsopgaver Som studentermedhjælper er din primære opgave at hjælpe ved kursusafvikling og forskning. Dine opgaver vil primært bestå af: Klargøring af operationsstuer til f.eks. kursusafvikling. Modtagelse og forberedelse af grise til anæstesi, herunder anlæggelse af venflon, urinkateter og intubering. Monitorering og prøvetagning under anæstesi. Operationsassisterende arbejde. Oprydning og rengøring ved kursets afslutning. Forefaldende opgaver relateret til laboratoriets daglige drift. Du refererer til Birgitte Saima Kousholt. Løn og forudsætninger Opgaven honoreres med timeløn svarende til SUL studentermedhjælpertakst (FAYL). Du vil modtage 1 times honorar for hver lektion, som du varetager. Alt fra 0 til 15 stimer om måneden. Hvem er du? For at blive studentermedhjælper, så er det en forudsætning, at du: er medicin- eller dyrlægestuderende, har gennemført et forsøgsdyrskursus, og har opnået erfaring fra De Kirurgiske Forskningslaboratorier i forbindelse med et forskningsår eller på anden måde har erfaring med bedøvelse af grise. Som person har du gode samarbejdsevner, er imødekommende og evner at bidrage til et godt arbejdsmiljø. Spørgsmål til stillingen Har du spørgsmål, er du velkommen til at kontakte Birgitte Saima Kousholt på: 23987790. Arbejdsstedet er Institut for Klinisk Medicin, Palle Juul-Jensens Boulevard 99, 8200 Aarhus N. Du kan blive indkaldt til en samtale inden for de næste to måneder. Ansættelsesgrundlag Ansættelse som studenterunderviser/instruktor forudsætter normalt, at den studerende har bestået de første 2 år af en relevant bacheloruddannelse eller tilsvarende niveau. Øvrige studerende kan ansættes, hvis institutionen vurderer, at den pågældende er fagligt kvalificeret til at varetage stillingen. Ansættelse og aflønning sker i henhold til Cirkulære om overenskomst for studenterundervisere ved universiteter mv. Ansøgning Din ansøgning skal indeholde følgende: Ansøgning Curriculum Vitae Angivelse af uddannelse (kopi af relevante eksamensbeviser) Referencer/anbefalinger kan uploades særskilt i e-rekrutteringssystemet Vi henviser til fakultetets Vejledning for ansøgere . Aarhus Universitet vil være en attraktiv og inspirerende arbejdsplads for alle og ønsker en kultur, hvor hver enkelt kan udfolde og udvikle sig. Vi ser ligestilling og diversitet som en ressource og opfordrer derfor alle interesserede til at ansøge. Ansøgning sendes via Aarhus Universitets rekrutteringssystem, som kan tilgås under stillingsopslaget på Aarhus Universitets hjemmeside. Questions about the position\n                            ? Birgitte Saima Kousholt Veterinarian, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Surgical Research Laboratories, SKS [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Health Administrative Centre - Health HR +4593521835 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Thursday 22 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CEST 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/postdoc-in-reimagining-brainbow-for-extracellular-vesicle-bioimaging": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Reimagining Brainbow for Extracellular Vesicle Bioimaging",
      "description": "Postdoc in Reimagining Brainbow for Extracellular Vesicle Bioimaging - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Health Postdoc in Reimagining Brainbow for Extracellular Vesicle Bioimaging Deadline 28 Oct 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Jan Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Health Universitetsbyen 81 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 1 Jan 2027 - 31 Dec 2028 ID: 170073 Apply Are you passionate about bioimaging and ready to tackle the innovative challenge of engineering rainbow-coloured extracellular vesicles? Then, the Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Aarhus University, invites you to apply for a 2-year postdoc position. Expected start date and duration of employment This is a 2-year position from 1 January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Job description The project is funded by Villum Foundation through the Villum Experiment grant From Genesis to Terminus: Rainbow-Painting of Extracellular Vesicles for Single-Particle Tracking . As a postdoc, you will primarily use cell cultures, and zebrafish embryos as a model organism, with the ambitious aim of developing innovative approaches in extracellular vesicle bioimaging. Through the project, you will be trained as an expert in the extracellular vesicle field with skills in genetic engineering of extracellular vesicles (including transient/stable transgenesis of zebrafish), live embryo imaging, and super-resolution imaging of cells. Your main tasks will consist of: Research of high international quality and publication in top journals. Collaboration with colleagues who work on extracellular vesicles and advanced bioimaging. Research-based supervision of Bachelor, Master and PhD students in a vibrant group. Your profile We are looking for a highly skilled and motivated person who are ready to take a risk and gain high through the Experiment grant. The candidate must have: A PhD degree in a relevant field (e.g. Molecular Biology, Cell Biology). A proven track record either in advanced bioimaging or extracellular vesicle biology. The successful candidate will have one or more of the followings: Expertise in super-resolution microscopy. Expertise in confocal/light-sheet microscopy of zebrafish embryos and image analysis. Experience with genetic engineering (plasmid construction and transfection). Experience in working with zebrafish or other animal models. Finally, we look for a candidate with: A high motivation and ambition in pursuing an academic career path. A strong collaborative spirit for working with colleagues and engaging with students. Excellent skills in communication and presentation. Fluency in spoken and written English. Who we are You will join a vibrant, collaborative, and international research community, where English is the primary language used for internal communication and teaching, and international candidates are not required to learn Danish. Aarhus University offers a wide range of services to support international researchers and their families, including career counselling for accompanying partners. You will be affiliated with an active research group led by Yuya Hayashi at the Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics. Yuya started his own group on extracellular vesicle biology and RNA nanotechnology funded by a Hallas-Møller Emerging Investigator grant from Novo Nordisk Foundation in 2022. Using the zebrafish as a model organism, the team focuses on studying the role of extracellular vesicles in cell-to-cell communication as inspiration for new nanomedicine designs based on the innovative \"RNA Origami\" technology. Visit his group webpage ( http://mbg.au.dk/yuya-hayashi/ ) for further information. Yuya also organises a cross-departmental network of extracellular vesicle researchers at Aarhus University, EVAnet ( http://mbg.au.dk/evanet/ ). What we offer The department offers: A well-developed research infrastructure, laboratories and access to shared equipment. An exciting interdisciplinary environment with many national, international and industrial collaborators. A research climate encouraging lively, open and critical discussion within and across different fields of research. A work environment with close working relationships, networking and social activities. A workplace characterised by professionalism, equality and a healthy work-life balance. Place of work and area of employment The place of work is Universitetsbyen 81, 8000 Aarhus C, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with related departments. The city of Aarhus In Aarhus you have easy access to beautiful nature, an exciting culture and city life as well as a safe environment for children - a great place for the whole family. The city of Aarhus has everything you need within a surprisingly small area: exciting national and international jobs, delightful residential areas, a rich cultural life, and beautiful surrounding landscape of woods and coastline that make Aarhus a wonderful place to live and work. See “life in Denmark” at Aarhus and surroundings (au.dk) for further details on the city and the university. Contact information For further information, please contact: Associate Professor, Yuya Hayashi ( [email protected] ). Deadline Applications must be received no later than 23 October 2026. Questions about the position\n                            ? Yuya Hayashi Associate Professor, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - Molecular Health +4587159712 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4593522463 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Wednesday 28 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/postdoc-position-in-laboratory-astrochemistry-1": {
      "title": "Postdoc Position in Laboratory Astrochemistry",
      "description": "Postdoc Position in Laboratory Astrochemistry - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Physics and Astronomy Postdoc Position in Laboratory Astrochemistry Deadline 28 Oct 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Mar Department of Physics and Astronomy Ny Munkegade 120 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 1 Mar 2027 - 28 Feb 2029 ID: 170177 Apply The Aarhus Laboratory Astrochemistry Group is seeking applications for a postdoctoral position in laboratory astrochemistry under supervision of Prof. Liv Hornekær at the Department of Physics and Astronomy at Aarhus University. Job description The successful applicants will participate in the experimental research activities under ERC Synergy Grant IRAstro and DNRF Center of Excellence for Interstellar Catalysis – InterCat. This combined project aims at elucidating how molecules on interstellar dust grain analogue surfaces organize, react and dissipate energy under low temperature and low pressure conditions mimicking dense interstellar dust and molecular clouds. The applicant will use low temperature scanning tunneling microscopy (STM), temperature programmed desorption, and (single molecule) IR spectroscopy to follow in situ reactions leading to complex molecule formation on realistic dust grain analogue surfaces. Close collaboration with theoreticians, observers and the experimental astrochemistry groups at Aarhus University and at the nodes of collaborative partners is expected. The job includes: Mapping of catalytic pathways and reaction rates on interstellar dust grain analogue surfaces using STM, TPD, and RAIRS. development, maintenance and troubleshooting on various experimental UHV setups participating in maintenance of the group laboratories. data analysis and writing scientific publications. supervision of PhD, Master and bachelor students. project administration, such as writing reports etc. Qualifications Candidates should have a PhD degree in physics or similar field, with strong experience in experimental surface science, UHV techniques, catalysis/reactions on surfaces and atomic scale characterization. A background in laboratory astrochemistry is preferred. The ideal candidate has good collaboration skills and is also able to work independently. About IRAstro - Molecular Quantum Dynamics in Low-Temperature Astrochemistry The ERC Synergy project IRAstro brings together leading researchers in physics, chemistry, and astrochemistry to uncover how molecules behave and react under the extreme conditions of interstellar space. Recent observations from the James Webb Space Telescope (JWST) reveal the complexity of low temperature molecular ices frozen out on interstellar dust grains in regions where new stars and planetary systems are formed. Interpreting these observations requires a deeper understanding of the fundamental physical and chemical processes that govern molecular behaviour at temperatures close to absolute zero. IRAstro addresses this challenge by combining cutting-edge laboratory experiments, advanced instrumentation, and first-principles theory. The project focuses on the quantum dynamics of molecules in low-temperature condensed phases - a frontier area essential for understanding how chemical complexity arises in space. https://phys.au.dk/irastro About InterCat – Center for Interstellar Catalysis InterCat is a center of excellence supported by the Danish National Research Foundation. The center is situated at the Department of Physics and Astronomy and at the Interdisciplinary Nanoscience Center at Aarhus University in Denmark, at Leiden Observatory at Leiden University in the Netherlands and Niels Bohr Institute at University of Copenhagen in Denmark. See https://phys.au.dk/intercat/ for further details. The scientific aim of the Center for Interstellar Catalysis is to determine whether the production of the molecular building blocks of life, e.g., sugars, amino acids, fats and DNA bases, predates the formation of stars and planets, and occurs at the extremely low temperatures and pressures found in interstellar space. InterCat thus aims to determine the molecular starting conditions for the origin of life across the universe. InterCat brings together research teams within surface science, nanoscience, heterogeneous catalysis and experimental and observational astrochemistry. Expected start date and duration of employment This is a 2-year postdoc position expected to start 1 March 2027 or as soon as possible. Contact information For further information, please contact: Prof. Liv Hornekær, [email protected] . Deadline Applications must be received no later than 28 October 2026. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the appointment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. All applicants will be notified whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee, and each applicant is given the opportunity to comment on the part of the assessment that concerns him/her self. Formalities and salary range Natural Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation . The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . Aarhus University also offers a Junior Researcher Development Programme targeted at career development for postdocs at AU. You can read more about it here . At the Faculty of Natural Science at Aarhus University, we strive to support our scientific staff in their career development. We focus on competency development and career clarification and want to make your opportunities transparent. On our website , you can find information on all types of scientific positions, as well as the entry criteria we use when assessing candidates. You can also read more about how we can assist you in your career planning and development. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Liv Hornekær Professor, Department of Physics and Astronomy +4561663133 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4520612514 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Wednesday 28 Oct 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
