    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/tenure-track-assistant-professor-associate-professor-positions-in-veternary-medicine": {
      "title": "Tenure track assistant professor/Associate professor positions in Veterinary medicine",
      "description": "Tenure track assistant professor/Associate professor positions in Veterinary medicine - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - Faculty: Technical Sciences Tenure track assistant professor/Associate professor positions in Veterinary medicine Deadline 3 Dec 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Aug Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences Blichers Allé 20 8830 Tjele Full-time position ID: 170541 Apply The Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences (ANIVET) is seeking three new staff members for teaching and research in veterinary medicine. The positions are available from 1 August 2027 or soon thereafter. The educational activities for these positions are aimed at students in veterinary medicine at both the bachelor’s and master’s levels. The veterinary medicine programme is organised into courses covering educationally relevant themes and integrates a range of disciplines, and this is done with the vision to create a professional engagement while ensuring scientific depth for the students of veterinary medicine. ANIVET is part of the Faculty of Technical Sciences at Aarhus University . The department is located near Viborg (Campus AU Viborg – Research Centre Foulum) and encompasses five research units with approximately 200 dedicated employees of which 50% are scientific staff. The AU Viborg campus will gradually grow to a student population of 800 – 900. The positions will be integrated into the department’s existing scientific research units, in which scientists at all career stages work together with skilled technical staff such as laboratory technicians and data analysts. The positions Clinical veterinary science – livestock Veterinary public health Veterinary pathology If you wish to apply for more than one position, please apply for each position separately.  Please read more down below in “How to apply”. 1. Tenure track assistant professor or Associated Professor in Clinical veterinary science – livestock We are seeking a candidate with a clinical background in veterinary science within production animals - Livestock. Research tasks The focus of the position is to: Perform clinical veterinary science within production animals, with emphasis on individual or group-level animal diagnostics, clinical decision-making, and evidence-based treatment and prevention strategies. Research in major production diseases in cattle and/or pigs of significant importance in Europe, including development of clinically applicable knowledge and tools supporting veterinary decision-making in practice. Integrate clinical findings with herd-level data to improve disease prevention and health management in modern production systems. Within his/her area of expertise, it is expected that in addition the candidate will: Conduct research-based advisory work for authorities and have an active role in externally funded research projects. Contribute to the development and delivery of teaching in clinical veterinary science for production animals, with emphasis on case-based and hands-on learning. Provide academic leadership within the clinical production animal field, including mentoring and coordination of junior teaching staff (e.g., assistant lecturers/teaching assistants). Contribute to strengthening collaboration with the veterinary profession and industry stakeholders in Denmark. Your profile The preferred candidate should demonstrate: The ability to independently conduct research within veterinary clinical science related to pig or cattle production Danish authorization as a veterinarian or can achieve it Preferably experiences within obstetrics 2. Tenure track assistant professor or Associated Professor in Veterinary Public Health We are seeking a candidate with strong expertise in veterinary public health, including popu-lation-level animal health, food safety/meat inspection, and the role of veterinarians in society. Research tasks The focus of the position is to : Conduct research within veterinary public health, including epidemiology, zoonoses, food safety/meat inspection, disease dynamics, risk assessment or animal welfare. Contribute to interdisciplinary One Health research integrating animal, human and environmental health on population level. Support evidence-based policy and advisory work for authorities. Participate in externally funded research projects. Within his/her area of expertise, it is expected that in addition the candidate will: Develop and deliver teaching in Veterinary Public Health for example to apply case-based and problem-oriented teaching methods with focus on real-world scenarios in veterinary services. Do research within monitoring of animal welfare issues across the EU. Contribute to teaching across the veterinary curriculum where public health perspectives are relevant. Your profile The preferred candidate should demonstrate: The ability to independently conduct research within veterinary public health preferably with an interdisciplinary research profile integrating biological, social and economic aspects in projects Danish authorization as a veterinarian or can achieve it. Experience with Danish conditions is an advantage. Preferably, experience with antimicrobial use at the population level. 3. Tenure track assistant professor or Associated Professor in Veterinary Pathology We are seeking a candidate with a broad background in veterinary pathology, encompassing both gross and histopathological examinations for diagnostic purposes with a strong interest in developing and innovating teaching within veterinary pathology. Research tasks The focus of the position is: General and comparative  veterinary pathology, including the mechanisms, diagnosis, and characterization of disease processes across animal species. Diagnostic pathology, encompassing post-mortem investigations, histopathology, and the integration of pathological findings into veterinary practice and meat inspection. Pathological assessment of animal welfare aspects of mortality in livestock Within his/her area of expertise, it is expected that in addition the candidate will : Teach and supervise students and early-career researchers at bachelor, master, and PhD levels. Conduct research-based advisory work for authorities and have an active role in externally funded research projects. Contribute to the collection and curation of pathological specimens for teaching purposes and reporting of findings to referring veterinarians and animal owners. Contribute to the continued development of the department's digital histopathology teaching platform, TUTOR. Support in the administration and further development of the department's animal donor programme for anatomy and pathology. Your profile The preferred candidate should have experience with: Post-mortem examinations, including diagnostic necropsies, case reporting, and communication of findings. Diagnostic histopathology. Your profle as Tenure Track assistant professor You are a skilled researcher with a solid background within your specific field of research, and you possess: Documented research qualifications at a high international level Teaching and supervision experience Qualifications for the Tenure-Track assistant professor level at Aarhus University must include postdoctoral training or similar with a relevant research profile and a strong scientific publication record in one or more of the areas of the position you are applying for. Please refer to the tenure track guidelines for the tenure review criteria and for the tenure review process. Your profile as Associate professor You are established as a prominent researcher within your specific field of research, and you possess: The ability to carry out independent and well-organized research work, as well as work as part of an interdisciplinary team. Documented teaching qualifications at a high international level. Experience with project management In order to be assessed as qualified as associate professor, you must meet the academic criteria as outlined here How to apply You must indicate the specific position you are applying for by selecting it in the menu. You may only select one position. If you wish to apply for one of the other positions, you must submit a separate application for each position. Please also indicate in your written application which position you are applying for. Furthermore, please indicate whether you are applying for a tenure-track assistant professor position, an associate professor position, or both  by ticking the box. . Who we are The Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences is well-known for its skilled and very innovative interdisciplinary research environments with a high international impact. We perform world-class research, which contributes with solutions to address essential societal challenges within the green transition; the food production and veterinary medicine – nationally and globally. The department generates novel research at the highest international level within sustainable food production, the environment, climate, and the health and welfare for animals and humans. The activities form the basis for our research-based public authority consultancy and degree programmes covering bachelor’s, master’s and PhD degree programmes within animal science and veterinary medicine. We offer a lively, engaged and innovative learning and study environment, which is closely integrated with the research environment. Our department has unique and advanced animal experimental research facilities and technologies located close to the research environment, and a comprehensive national and international research network and strong industrial and professional collaborations. What we offer A well-developed research infrastructure, laboratories and access to shared equipment and animal experimental facilities. An informal and multicultural research environment with high professionalism and close collaboration and networking activities. A workplace characterised by equality and a good work-life balance, and open discussions across different fields of research. Living in Denmark Please visit the international staff https://internationalstaff.au.dk/prearrival/ for information about arriving to and living in Denmark for both the applicants and their potential families. Area of employment and place of work The area of employment is Aarhus University (AU), with related departments The place of work is AU Viborg, Research Centre Foulum, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Blichers Allé 20, DK-8830 Tjele. AU Viborg is approximately 10 km from Viborg. You can read more about it here: https://international.viborg.dk/ Contact For further information, please contact Deputy head of department, Professor Henrik Callesen ( [email protected] ) or Head of department, Professor Charlotte Lauridsen ( [email protected] ) Technical Sciences Tenure Track Aarhus University offers talented scientists from around the world attractive career perspectives via the Technical Sciences Tenure Track Programme. Highly qualified candidates are appointed as Assistant Professors for a period of six years with the prospect of performance- based advancement to a tenured Associate Professorship. The aim of the Technical Sciences Tenure Track Programme is to: attract outstanding talented individuals that are competitive at an international level to promote the early development of independent research success early in the career of scientists to create transparency in the academic career path As part of the tenure track position, the candidate is offered: access to research infrastructure capability development, including postgraduate teacher training a mentoring programme support to develop scientific networks and to secure interdisciplinary research at the highest level As part of the Aarhus University Tenure Track Programme, the University carries out a mid-way evaluation to review the progress of the tenure track candidate after three years, according to the same criteria used in the final tenure review. The final tenure review is conducted after five and a half years. If the review is positive, the candidate will be offered a tenured position as Associate Professor at Aarhus University. Please refer to the tenure track guidelines for the tenure review criteria and for the tenure review process. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the assessment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. The selection is made on the basis of an assessment of who of the candidates are most relevant considering the requirements of the advertisement. All applicants will be notified within 6 weeks whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee and will receive his/her assessment. Formalities and salary range Technical Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation. The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website . Questions about the position\n                            ? Henrik Callesen Professor, Deputy Head of Dept. for Research and Talent developm, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences +4520803435 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4593522463 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Thursday  3 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/tenure-track-assistant-professor-associate-professor-position-in-materials-science-and-engineering": {
      "title": "Tenure track Assistant professor/Associate professor Position in Materials Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Tenure track Assistant professor/Associate professor Position in Materials Science and Engineering - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering - Manufacturing and Mechatronics - Faculty: Technical Sciences Tenure track Assistant professor/Associate professor Position in Materials Science and Engineering Deadline 8 Dec 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Jul Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering - Manufacturing and Mechatronics Katrinebjergvej 89F 8200 Aarhus N Full-time position ID: 170995 Apply Aarhus University, Denmark The Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering at Aarhus University invites applications for two positions at the rank of: •    Tenure Track Assistant Professor, or •    Associate Professor The positions are offered within the broad field of Materials Engineering and Manufacturing, with a particular focus on participating in the department’s research and education in materials engineering, durability, emerging and advanced materials, advanced manufacturing and surface engineering. The department seeks candidates who will help shape a modern materials science profile, in research as well as in teaching, and who have demonstrated relevant experience in the field. Expected start date July 1st, 2027, or as soon as possible. Research Areas We welcome applicants with a solid background in materials science and engineering, mechanical engineering, materials-focused chemical engineering, applied physics, or closely related disciplines. We particularly encourage applications within, but not limited to, the following research themes: Additive and hybrid manufacturing Including metal additive manufacturing, laser-based processing and welding, joining of metallic and dissimilar materials, post-processing, surface engineering, and process characterisation and modelling. Materials durability and advanced materials Including materials under demanding and extreme conditions, 4D printing, bioprinting, and biofabrication, surface modification, lubrication technologies and functional surfaces. Applicants are expected to contribute to both f undamental understanding and applied solutions , with relevance to engineering systems and industrial applications Research and Teaching Responsibilities The selected candidates will: •    Teach, contribute to, and develop courses in materials science and engineering, additive manufacturing, and manufacturing processes at different levels, from foundational bachelor’s courses to specialized master’s and PhD courses •    Contribute directly to the further development of the materials and manufacturing science curriculum at different program levels •    Supervise bachelor’s, master’s, and PhD students •    Attract external research funding •    Engage in knowledge exchange with industry and research partners •    Participate in departmental and university service activities Your Profile We are looking for candidates who can contribute to research, education, and innovation at an international level. To meet expectations in this role, we expect the candidate to fulfill the following requirements: -    A PhD in materials science and engineering, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field -    Substantial experience conducting high-quality research in materials science and engineering, with publications in leading international journals that match career stage -    Experience in at least one of the research areas listed above, along with familiarity with experimental, computational, or theoretical research methods -    Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration across engineering disciplines and with industry -    For the positions as associate professor, the applicants should, in addition, have: -    Documented teaching experience and a clear commitment to teaching and advancing materials science courses, from introductory undergraduate instruction through master’s and PhD-level study -    For associate professor applicants: a documented record of self-directed research leadership, external funding acquisition, supervision of PhD students, and teaching and course development at university level Who we are The engineering field in Aarhus University is evolving with a rapid growth in student population, major research initiatives as well as through the establishment of a number of new physical facilities in the city center of Aarhus. We have comprehensive plans for increased activities in research and education, as well as public and industrial cooperation. The  Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering within the Faculty of Technical Sciences has cooperation with universities and advisory service providers in more than 20 countries. The engineering field at Aarhus University is well established with extensive research activities, over 700 mechanical engineering students and a long tradition of industrial cooperation that we wish to extend significantly. What we offer The department offers: -    research infrastructure, laboratories and access to shared equipment -    an exciting interdisciplinary environment with many national, international and industrial collaborators -    a research climate encouraging lively, open and critical discussion within and across different fields of research -    a work environment with close working relationships, networking and social activities -    a workplace characterized by professionalism, equality and a healthy work-life balance Place of work and area of employment The place of employment is Aarhus University, and the place of work is Mechanical and Production Engineering, Katrinebjergvej 89, DK-8200 Aarhus N, Denmark. Contact information For more information about the position contact Head of Section of Manufacturing and Mechatronics, Professor Ramin Aghababaei ( [email protected] / +45 9350 8956) or Head of Section of Mechanics and Materials, Professor Michal Kazimierz Budzik ( [email protected] , +45 4189 3217) Deadline Applications must be received no later than December 8th, 2026. Technical Sciences Tenure Track Aarhus University offers talented scientists from around the world attractive career perspectives via the Technical Sciences Tenure Track Programme. Highly qualified candidates are appointed as Assistant Professors for a period of six years with the prospect of performance- based advancement to a tenured Associate Professorship. The aim of the Technical Sciences Tenure Track Programme is to: attract outstanding talented individuals that are competitive at an international level to promote the early development of independent research success early in the career of scientists to create transparency in the academic career path As part of the tenure track position, the candidate is offered: access to research infrastructure capability development, including postgraduate teacher training a mentoring programme support to develop scientific networks and to secure interdisciplinary research at the highest level As part of the Aarhus University Tenure Track Programme, the University carries out a mid-way evaluation to review the progress of the tenure track candidate after three years, according to the same criteria used in the final tenure review. The final tenure review is conducted after five and a half years. If the review is positive, the candidate will be offered a tenured position as Associate Professor at Aarhus University. Please refer to the tenure track guidelines for the tenure review criteria and for the tenure review process. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the assessment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. The selection is made on the basis of an assessment of who of the candidates are most relevant considering the requirements of the advertisement. All applicants will be notified within 6 weeks whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee and will receive his/her assessment. Formalities and salary range Technical Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation. The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website . Questions about the position\n                            ? Ramin Aghababaei Head of Section, Professor, Department of Mechanical and Production Engineering - Manufacturing and Mechatronics +4593508956 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4593521962 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Tuesday  8 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
