      "description": "Center for Rusmiddelforskning søger 4-5 studentermedhjælpere til ansættelse i Aarhus - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences - Centre for Alcohol and Drug Research Center for Rusmiddelforskning søger 4-5 studentermedhjælpere til ansættelse i Aarhus Deadline 8 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Dec Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences - Centre for Alcohol and Drug Research Bartholins Allé 10 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term part-time position 1 Dec 2026 - 30 Nov 2029 8 hours per week ID: 171368 Apply Center for Rusmiddelforskning, Aarhus Universitet søger 4-5 studentermedhjælpere primært til transskribering af kvalitative interviews, der er lavet i forbindelse med forskningsprojekter på centret. Indimellem har vi projekter, som kan være andet arbejde end transskriberinger. Ansættelsesperioden er på op til 3 år, dog kun så længe du studerer. Center for Rusmiddelforskning udfører samfundsvidenskabelig forskning på rusmiddelområdet. Du kan læse om centrets forskningsområder på hjemmesiden . Du skal være i gang med en lang videregående uddannelse og gerne have kendskab til kvalitative metoder. Du får stillet en computer til rådighed og kan selv tilrettelægge dit arbejde og hvorfra du arbejder. Kontaktinfo Yderligere oplysninger om stillingerne kan indhentes hos centersekretær Annette Bang Rasmussen, e-mail: [email protected] Hvis du har behov for hjælp til at uploade din ansøgning eller har spørgsmål vedr. rekrutteringsprocessen, bedes du kontakte HR koordinator Charlotte Thomsen, e-mail: [email protected] Praktisk info Den gennemsnitlige ugentlige arbejdstid vil være max. 8 timer, og arbejdsstedet er Center for Rusmiddelforskning, Aarhus Universitet, Bartholins Allé 9, 8000 Aarhus C. Ansøgningen skal sendes elektronisk og være os i hænde senest den 8. november 2026 Tiltrædelse 1. december 2026 eller snarest muligt. Send os en kortfattet ansøgning, vedlagt indskrivningsbekræftelse og CV Krav og vilkår Du ansættes efter fællesoverenskomsten mellem Finansministeriet og Offentlige Ansattes Organisation – Det Statslige Område (OAO-S-fællesoverenskomsten) samt organisationsaftale for kontorfunktionærer, laboranter og IT-medarbejdere (HK). Du indplaceres som kontorfunktionær i løngruppe 2-3 afhængigt af uddannelse og kvalifikationer. Aarhus Universitet Aarhus Universitet vil være en attraktiv og inspirerende arbejdsplads for alle og ønsker en kultur, hvor hver enkelt kan udfolde og udvikle sig. Vi ser ligestilling og diversitet som en ressource og opfordrer derfor alle interesserede til at ansøge . Ansøgning sendes via Aarhus Universitets rekrutteringssystem, som kan tilgås under stillingsopslaget på Aarhus Universitets hjemmeside. Questions about the position\n                            ? Annette Bang Rasmussen Centre Secretary, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences - Centre for Alcohol and Drug Research +4523266332 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Aarhus BSS Administrative Centre - Aarhus BSS HR and PhD Administration +4593509350 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Sunday  8 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/ai-developer-for-validation-and-clinical-implementation-of-ai-systems-in-radiology": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "AI-udvikler til validering og klinisk implementering af AI-systemer inden for radiologi - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology AI-udvikler til validering og klinisk implementering af AI-systemer inden for radiologi Deadline 9 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Jan Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology Palle Juul-Jensens Boulevard 99 8200 Aarhus N Fixed term full-time position 1 Jan 2027 - 31 Dec 2028 ID: 171406 Apply The Department of Clinical Medicine at the Faculty of Health, Aarhus University, invites applications for a position as AI Developer for validation and clinical implementation of AI systems, commencing on 1 January 2027, preferably before then, if possible. The position is a fixed-term full-time appointment until 31 December 2028 which aligns with the end date of the project related to the grant agreement. AURA is the radiology research unit at Aarhus University Hospital and is affiliated with the Department of Clinical Medicine at Aarhus University. We conduct research across a broad range of radiological topics and work closely with clinical departments on projects spanning classical statistical methods, artificial intelligence, language models, and advanced image analysis. In recent years, we have expanded our activities within AI and are therefore seeking additional expertise for both existing and new projects. As an AI Developer in AURA, you will play a central role in validating, implementing, and further developing AI solutions for use in healthcare. You will become part of an ambitious research environment with close collaboration between researchers, clinicians, and technical specialists, and you will have the opportunity to influence both projects and your own role. As an AI Developer at the Department of Clinical Medicine, you will become part of what is likely the largest health sciences research institute in Denmark. Clinical research covers all medical specialties and is carried out in close collaboration with the university hospital and regional hospitals in the Central Denmark Region. We have approximately 30,000 square metres of modern research facilities for experimental surgery and medicine, animal facilities, and advanced scanners. The department has overall responsibility for the Master’s degree programmes in Medicine and Molecular Medicine. The department comprises approximately 670 academic staff members, 500 PhD students, and 160 technical and administrative staff, all working collaboratively across disciplines. As an AI Developer, you will be based at Aarhus University Hospital in the Central Denmark Region. You can read more about the department here and about the faculty here . Your Job Responsibilities As an AI Developer, your primary responsibilities will be to develop, validate, and implement AI solutions for clinical use, while supporting the research group's activities within data analysis, software development, and advanced image analysis. You will contribute to research and development activities through technical development, project work, and interdisciplinary collaboration. In your daily work, you will collaborate closely with researchers, clinicians, students, and external partners. Your tasks will primarily include: Validation and implementation of AI systems for clinical use. Development, testing, and evaluation of new AI solutions. Software development and data analysis related to research and development projects. Establishment and maintenance of technical workflows and development environments. Responsibility for your own technical sub-projects and development processes. Providing technical and methodological support and advice to researchers and clinicians. Co-supervision and academic support of Master's and PhD students. Collaboration with external partners, including companies and healthcare stakeholders. Contributing to the establishment of new research and development projects within AI and radiology. The position offers a high degree of independence, and we would like you to help shape the content of the role so that it matches your competencies, interests, and career goals. You will report to Clinical Professor, Department Chair of Radiology, Ole Graumann. Your Qualifications You hold a Master's degree in a relevant field, such as computer science, software development, physics, engineering, or a related discipline. We expect that you: Have strong competencies in programming and software development. Are familiar with Linux and command-line based work. Have experience with AI development or similar technical development work. Are able to work independently and drive technical projects and sub-projects. Enjoy collaborating with and supporting researchers and students in their projects. It is an advantage if you have experience with: Research projects or research collaborations. Healthcare data, medical image analysis, or clinical AI systems. Supervision, teaching, or academic mentoring. Your educational background is less important than your technical competencies, experience, and ability to translate technical solutions into practical applications within a clinical environment. As a person, you possess strong collaborative skills, demonstrate initiative, and are able to drive progress in complex projects. You thrive in an interdisciplinary environment and contribute positively to a good working environment. We expect you to speak and write English fluently. We Offer A strong and ambitious research environment with close ties to clinical practice. Significant influence over your own projects and responsibilities. The opportunity to shape the development and implementation of AI solutions in healthcare. The opportunity to co-supervise Master's and PhD students. Excellent opportunities for professional development within AI, software development, and clinical implementation. An interdisciplinary environment with close collaboration between researchers, clinicians, and technical specialists. Questions About the Position If you have any questions about the position, you are welcome to contact MD, PhD, and External Lecturer Mathis Rasmussen by telephone at +45 23 80 42 10 or by email at [email protected] . The place of work is AURA, Department of Radiology, Aarhus University Hospital, Palle Juul-Jensens Boulevard 99, DK-8200 Aarhus N, Denmark. The application deadline is Monday the 9th of November 2026. We expect to conduct interviews Monday the 23rd of November 2026. A second interview, if required, is expected to take place on Wednesday, 25th of November 2026. As part of the recruitment process, you may be asked to complete a short professional case assignment. Terms of employment Salary and terms of employment are governed by the collective agreement for Academics in the State, Nurses in the State or Nurses and radiographers with a master’s degree. Academics in the State will be appointed at basic salary grade 4–8. For the right candidate, appointment as Senior Consultant will be possible, with remuneration in accordance with Appendix 4 of the collective agreement. Nurses in the State will be appointed at basic salary grade 1-3, and Nurses and radiographers with a master’s degree will be appointed at basic salary grade 1-8. Application Your application must include the following: Motivated application Curriculum Vitae Indication of education (a copy of the diplomas should be uploaded) References/recommendations can be uploaded separately in the recruitment system We refer to the faculty’s Guideline for applicants . Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Ole Graumann Clinical Professor, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Health Administrative Centre - Health HR +4521623283 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Monday  9 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/academic-staff-member-ac-bachelor-within-ai-and-radiology-for-the-department-of-radiology-10-hours-per-week": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "Academic Staff Member (AC-Bachelor) within AI and Radiology for the Department of Radiology (10 Hours per Week) - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology Academic Staff Member (AC-Bachelor) within AI and Radiology for the Department of Radiology (10 Hours per Week) Deadline 9 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Jan Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology Palle Juul-Jensens Boulevard 99 8200 Aarhus N Fixed term part-time position 1 Jan 2027 - 31 Aug 2028 10 hours per week ID: 171424 Apply The Department of Clinical Medicine at the Faculty of Health, Aarhus University, invites applications for a position as an academic staff member (AC Bachelor) within AI and Radiology, commencing on 1 January 2027, preferably before then, if possible. The position is a part-time appointment of 10 hours per week. The employment is for a fixed term until the 31 of August 2028 which aligns with period 1 and 2 of the project according to the grant agreement. AURA is the radiology research unit at Aarhus University Hospital and is affiliated with the Department of Clinical Medicine at Aarhus University. We conduct research across a broad range of radiological topics and work closely with clinical departments on projects spanning classical statistical methods, artificial intelligence, language models, and advanced image analysis. Are you a student of medicine or the natural sciences with an interest in AI, research, and clinical data? As an academic staff member (Bachelor's Degree) in AURA, you will become part of a strong research environment where you will work on cutting-edge projects within AI and radiology. You will have the opportunity to contribute to scientific publications and develop your competencies within research, data analysis, and AI. As an academic staff member (Bachelor's Degree) at the Department of Clinical Medicine, you will become part of what is likely the largest health sciences research institute in Denmark. Clinical research covers all medical specialties and is carried out in close collaboration with the university hospital and regional hospitals in the Central Denmark Region. We have approximately 30,000 square metres of modern research facilities for experimental surgery and medicine, animal facilities, and advanced scanners. The department has overall responsibility for the Master's degree programmes in Medicine and Molecular Medicine. The department comprises approximately 670 academic staff members, 500 PhD students, and 160 technical and administrative staff working collaboratively across disciplines. As an academic staff member (Bachelor's Degree), you will be based at Aarhus University Hospital in the Central Denmark Region. You can read more about the department here and about the faculty here . Your Job Responsibilities As an academic staff member (Bachelor's Degree), your primary responsibilities will be to contribute to research within AI, clinical data, and advanced image analysis, and to support the development of new research projects within AURA. Your tasks will primarily include: Applying Large Language Models (LLMs) to extract structured information from radiology reports and clinical records. Contributing to research and quality improvement projects based on clinical data. Developing and validating AI-based methods for osteoporosis screening using conventional X-ray images. Collaborating with an external industry partner. Participating in new AI and radiology projects that are continuously being developed within the research group. Contributing to the preparation of scientific publications based on project results, with opportunities for both first authorship and co-authorship. Participating in group meetings, journal clubs, and other academic activities. You will become part of an engaged research environment and will work closely with researchers, clinicians, and fellow students. At the same time, you will have the opportunity to influence the development and direction of the projects. You will report to Clinical Professor of Radiology Ole Graumann. Your Qualifications You are enrolled in a medical or natural sciences degree programme at Master's level and have an interest in research, AI, and data analysis. It is an advantage if you are in the early stages of your Master studies. We expect that you: Are motivated to contribute to the projects of others. Are able to be physically present at the research unit when compatible with your studies. Participate actively in group meetings, journal clubs, and other academic activities whenever possible. Are curious, engaged, and motivated to develop as a researcher. It is an advantage if you have: Experience with language models or other AI methods. Experience with programming, scripting, or statistical analysis. Experience in writing scientific publications. Knowledge of Linux and command-line based work. If you lack experience in some of these areas, we still encourage you to apply. As a person, you possess strong collaborative skills, demonstrate initiative, and contribute positively to a strong academic environment. We Offer 10 hours per week with flexible organisation of working hours. A strong and ambitious research environment. Opportunities for co-authorship and, where relevant, first authorship. Close academic mentoring and collaboration with researchers and clinicians. Opportunities for continued collaboration, including a research year or Master's thesis project within the research group. Questions About the Position If you have any questions about the position, please contact MD, PhD, and External Lecturer Mathis Rasmussen by telephone at +45 23 80 42 10. The place of work is AURA, Department of Radiology, Aarhus University Hospital, Palle Juul-Jensens Boulevard 99, DK-8200 Aarhus N, Denmark. The application deadline is Monday the 9th of November 2026. We expect to conduct interviews Monday the 23rd of November 2026. Terms of employment Salary and terms of employment are governed by the collective agreement for Academics in the State. You will be appointed at basic salary grade 1–6. Application Your application must include the following: Motivated application Curriculum Vitae Indication of education (a copy of the diplomas should be uploaded) References/recommendations can be uploaded separately in the recruitment system We refer to the faculty’s Guideline for applicants . Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Ole Graumann Clinical Professor, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Radiology [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Health Administrative Centre - Health HR +4521623283 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Monday  9 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
