    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-instructors-for-hacky-hours-study-cafe": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "Student Instructors for Hacky Hours Study Cafe - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact School of Culture and Society - History, subject Student Instructors for Hacky Hours Study Cafe Deadline 12 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Feb School of Culture and Society - History, subject Jens Chr. Skous Vej 5 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term part-time position 1 Feb 2027 - 31 May 2027 2 hours per week ID: 171572 Apply We are looking for two dedicated and academically strong student instructors to support fellow history students working independently on digital projects in relevant courses like Kildenært emne or BA-projects. The support will take place through a hacky hour study café in the library/Nobelsalen,  two hours a week (usually Friday 12-14 or 14-16;  26 hours in total). The Hacky Hour Study Café is meant to support the use of tools introduced in DAM in other courses and student projects. Employment period 1 February – 31 May 2027. Responsibilities As a student instructor, you will: Help students contextualize and apply the tools (Voyant, Transkribus, R, OpenRefine, regex, spreadsheets and their Ucloud variants) introduced in DAM to new projects. Assist with troubleshooting their machines and support their understanding of core concepts. Guide students in working on their own project. Demonstrate best digital practices and foster the development of computational thinking. In short: “Teach students how to fish – and occasionally hand out a free fish.” We expect that you: Have completed the DAM or similar course with good results. Are interested in teaching and motivated to help others understand complex topics. Are patient, approachable, and able to communicate technical material in an accessible way. We offer: A stimulating and rewarding student job where you strengthen both your academic and teaching skills. An inspiring learning environment where you can make a real difference for your fellow students. Please contact Kathrine Juul Svejstrup [email protected] for more information about the position. A prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is an actively enrolled student. Employment is subject to the availability of the necessary funding. Applicants will be notified of the outcome of their application within four weeks of the application deadline. Application Please upload a short motivated application and your CV. Terms of Employment Employment is in accordance with the Ministry of Finance and SUL Finansministeriet og SUL (student instructors). The application must include a copy of your diploma and any documentation of previous teaching experience. Aarhus University aims to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for everyone and strives for a culture where each individual can thrive and develop. We view equality and diversity as valuable resources and therefore encourage all interested candidates to apply. About Arts The Faculty of Arts is one of Northern Europe’s most significant faculties for research and higher education in the humanities, theology and education. Within this broad academic scope, the faculty comprises approximately 700 researchers, 200 PhD students, 9,000 Bachelor’s and Master’s degree students, and 1,500 further and continuing education students. We believe that the best ideas arise when different perspectives meet – and that research, teaching and innovation are best developed in dialogue with the surrounding society. You can find more information here: Faculty of Arts | Aarhus Universitet The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Kathrine Juul Svejstrup Department Consultant, School of Culture and Society - Culture and Society, Local secretariat 1443 +4587159732 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Arts Administrative Centre - Arts HR +4523382165 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Thursday 12 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-assistants-for-digital-archives-and-methods-spring-2027": {
      "title": "Questions about the position ?",
      "description": "Student assistants for Digital Archives and Methods, spring 2027 - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact School of Culture and Society - History, subject Student assistants for Digital Archives and Methods, spring 2027 Deadline 12 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 8 Feb School of Culture and Society - History, subject Jens Chr. Skous Vej 5 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term part-time position 8 Feb 2027 -  7 May 2027 4 hours per week ID: 171575 Apply Introduction to Digital Archives and Methods is a moderately computationally intensive standalone course in History BA. This course is scheduled on Tuesdays 8 -12 and Thursdays 10 - 14 in weeks 6 - 20. The bulk of assistance is needed in Weeks 6 - 15 in a minimum of 4 hr intervals. Each class is attended by circa 50-60 students who work in groups to complete digital tasks. The course is in-person. We are looking for 2 teaching student assistants who can support the learners in this course through troubleshooting, assistance and conceptual guidance on the main tasks and themes of the course. The tasks of the assistants are to provide in-class/remote assistance (in class-time): · setup: assist with local software installations or online instantiations of Voyant, Transkribus, UCloud, R, OpenRefine, etc. access to course sources and computational environments · operation: help students operate the tools introduced in the course and guide students in the pursuit of course tasks. Help interpret tool outputs during the conceptual work towards assessments. Act as student liaisons, translating student needs into technical questions for the instructors. Selected candidates should show initiative, be digitally savvy and enthusiastic as well as reliable and well-organized. The work requires independence, flexibility, and attention to detail. Furthermore, the candidate should have good interpersonal skills. The ideal candidate's application should demonstrate the following qualifications: Good command of English and Danish, both oral and written Familiarity with the course materials as well as the digital tools introduced: previous attendance of Digital Archives and Methods or equivalent is recommended. Experience with troubleshooting code and a knack for digital problem-solving Proactive, motivated and enthusiastic attitude Ability to communicate effectively with students and fellow assistants, as well as liaise with instructors. Please contact Kathrine Juul Svejstrup [email protected] for more information about the positions. Applications should address how the applicant fits the qualifications listed above, be written in English and accompanied by a brief CV. Please indicate your availability in class time in weeks 6 to 15 and state which operating systems you are comfortable troubleshooting. A prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is an actively enrolled student. Employment is subject to the availability of the necessary funding. Applicants will be notified of the outcome of their application within four weeks of the application deadline. Terms of Employment Employment is in accordance with the Ministry of Finance and SUL Finansministeriet og SUL (student instructors). The application must include a copy of your diploma and any documentation of previous teaching experience. Aarhus University aims to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for everyone and strives for a culture where each individual can thrive and develop. We view equality and diversity as valuable resources and therefore encourage all interested candidates to apply. About Arts The Faculty of Arts is one of Northern Europe’s most significant faculties for research and higher education in the humanities, theology and education. Within this broad academic scope, the faculty comprises approximately 700 researchers, 200 PhD students, 9,000 Bachelor’s and Master’s degree students, and 1,500 further and continuing education students. We believe that the best ideas arise when different perspectives meet – and that research, teaching and innovation are best developed in dialogue with the surrounding society. You can find more information here: Faculty of Arts | Aarhus Universitet The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Kathrine Juul Svejstrup Department Consultant, School of Culture and Society - Culture and Society, Local secretariat 1443 +4587159732 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Arts Administrative Centre - Arts HR +4523382165 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Thursday 12 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/student-assistant-as-administrative-assistant-in-project-management-office-at-au-herning-1": {
      "title": "Student Assistant as Administrative Assistant in Project Management Office",
      "description": "Student Assistant as Administrative Assistant in Project Management Office at AU Herning - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Business Development and Technology Student Assistant as Administrative Assistant in Project Management Office at AU Herning Deadline 15 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Dec Department of Business Development and Technology Birk Centerpark 15 7400 Herning Fixed term part-time position 1 Dec 2026 - 30 Nov 2029 8 hours per week ID: 171317 Apply The Project Management Office at AU Herning is looking for a student assistant to carry out various administration projects as they relate to various research projects, project administration, and course administration at AU Herning. We are looking for a student assistant who can assist with the following tasks: Various administration tasks with the PMO team Administration work on different research grants, both within Denmark and the EU Daily administrative tasks using Microsoft Suite, Adobe, and other programs SOME management for international research projects Regular communication with international partners for research projects Regular administrative tasks such as data entry, data gathering, and testing interfaces. Assistant with planning and working events hosted by the department Who we are looking for: You must be enrolled at AU Herning You must thrive in an environment where precision and accuracy is important, and you can stay focused and selfdirected on various tasks You have good analytical skills Have a good grasp on the English language Who we are BTECH is part of Aarhus BSS, Aarhus University – a top 100 university. Aarhus BSS has achieved the triple-crown AASCB, AMBA and EQUIS accreditations. BTECH is located in the business-oriented and entrepreneurial city of Herning. The department excels in business, IT and engineering disciplines and emphasises the importance of company collaborations. We have around 1,200 students and close to 100 academic staff members. Each year, approximately 500 students are involved in company projects in more than 250 companies ranging from SMEs to leading multinationals. Our incubator Business Factory launches 10 new companies each year. We influence society through business development and technology. For this reason, many research projects are conducted in close collaboration with industry on the basis of new data and new technologies. These projects are generously supported by the ERC, Horizon Europe, the Independent Research Fund Denmark and the Danish Industry Foundation, among others. More information about BTECH is available here . Further information For further information about the position and the department, please contact Emily Tynes: tel. +45 4189 3353; email [email protected] If you need help uploading your application or have any questions about the recruitment process, please contact HR Supporter, Charlotte Thomsen, tel.: +45 8716 5362; email: [email protected] . Practical information Starting date as soon as possible and no later than 1 December 2025. The average number of working hours is 8 hours weekly. The place of work is Birk Centerpark 15, 7400 Herning It is a permanent position which means for as long as you are a student. Application deadline 15 November 2026 Application If you are interested in applying for the position, please send: A short motivated application CV Enrolment certification Terms of employment You will be employed as an hourly-paid student assistant under the collective agreement between the Danish Ministry of Finance and the Organisations of Public Employees – Denmark (OAO-S Collective Agreement, State Sector), as well as the organisational agreement for clerical employees, laboratory technicians and IT staff (HK). Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Aarhus University Aarhus University is an academically diverse and research-intensive university with a strong commitment to high-quality research and education and the development of society nationally and globally. The university offers an inspiring research and teaching environment to its 37,000 students (FTEs) and 8,700 employees and has an annual revenue of EUR 1.106 billion. Learn more at www.international.au.dk/ Questions about the position\n                            ? Emily Tynes Project Manager, Department of Business Development and Technology +4541893353 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Aarhus BSS Administrative Centre - Aarhus BSS HR and PhD Administration +4593509350 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Sunday 15 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
