    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/postdoctoral-position-in-stakeholder-and-consumer-research": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Position in Stakeholder and Consumer Research",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Position in Stakeholder and Consumer Research - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Food Science - Food Quality Perception & Society - Faculty: Technical Sciences Postdoctoral Position in Stakeholder and Consumer Research Deadline 16 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Jan Department of Food Science - Food Quality Perception & Society Agro Food Park 48 8200 Aarhus N Fixed term full-time position 1 Jan 2027 - 31 Dec 2028 ID: 171699 Apply Aarhus University invites applications for a postdoctoral position in Stakeholder and Consumer Research within the Food Quality Perception and Society (FQS) science team. The position is embedded in a portfolio of European research and innovation projects addressing sustainable packaging, food labelling and circularity. A central focus will be to understand consumer and stakeholder needs and translate these insights into research and development of packaging and food labelling solutions that promote sustainable consumption and production, strengthen circularity, and inform communication strategies to enhance consumer awareness, engagement and adoption. The postdoc will work across several EU-funded projects, including among others BIOWRAP (funded by the Circular Bio-based Europe Joint Undertaking, CBE JU), Environmental Food Label (funded by EIT Food), and CIRC4FOOD (funded by Horizon Europe). Research and responsibilities The postdoc will conduct and coordinate stakeholder and consumer research , with particular emphasis on qualitative and mixed-method approaches, including: stakeholder mapping, interviews, focus groups, workshops and co-creation; consumer research on perceptions, needs, barriers, motivations and adoption; translating research insights into product, packaging and labelling innovation; engaging industry, consumers, policymakers and other stakeholders throughout the research and innovation process; designing and implementing consumer engagement and communication actions to raise awareness, encourage participation, share research findings and promote the uptake of sustainable solutions; developing accessible, targeted and audience-appropriate communication materials and activities, including consumer-facing content, dissemination events and interactive engagement formats; collaborating with technical, regulatory and interdisciplinary experts to integrate consumer and stakeholder insights with product specifications, user needs, and relevant legislative and regulatory requirements, supporting the development of sustainable and feasible solutions. leading and contributing to scientific publications, project deliverables and research communication; and identifying new research questions, collaborations and opportunities for future EU and national funding . Qualifications Applicants must have: a PhD degree or equivalent in consumer science, social sciences, psychology, behavioural science, sociology, anthropology, marketing/ business, food science -with a focus on consumer science, culture or systems-, science communication or a related discipline; documented experience in consumer and/or stakeholder research ; experience designing and conducting qualitative research , such as interviews, focus groups, workshops or co-creation; strong statistical skills and experience in data analysis and interpretation of various methods; strong analytical and scientific writing skills, with a track record of peer-reviewed publications; experience working independently and collaboratively in interdisciplinary and international research teams ; excellent written and spoken English; and strong organisational and communication skills. Experience with mixed-method research, sustainable consumption, product or packaging innovation, environmental labelling, food research, public engagement, open science, EU-funded projects or external funding development will be considered an advantage. Profile and opportunities We are looking for an independent, collaborative and creative researcher able to work across disciplines and engage effectively with consumers, industry, researchers and societal stakeholders. The position offers an opportunity to develop a research profile at the intersection of consumer and stakeholder science, sustainable solution design, innovation and societal impact , while contributing to high-profile European research projects and developing new research collaborations and funding opportunities. Expected start date and duration of employment This is a 2–year position from 1 January 2027, or as soon possible thereafter. Place of work and area of employment The place of work is Agro Food Park 48, 8200 Aarhus N, and the area of employment is Aarhus University with related departments. Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the appointment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. All applicants will be notified whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee, and each applicant is given the opportunity to comment on the part of the assessment that concerns him/her self. Formalities and salary range Technical Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation . The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . Aarhus University also offers a Junior Researcher Development Programme targeted at career development for postdocs at AU. You can read more about it here . The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Derek V. Byrne Professor, Head of Section, Department of Food Science - Food Quality Perception & Society +4528782840 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR +4520968189 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Monday 16 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/four-year-researcher-position-on-greenland-marine-ecosystems": {
      "title": "Four-year Researcher position on Greenland marine ecosystems",
      "description": "Four-year Researcher position on Greenland marine ecosystems - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact Department of Ecoscience - Marine Ecology - Faculty: Technical Sciences Four-year Researcher position on Greenland marine ecosystems Deadline 18 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 15 Feb Department of Ecoscience - Marine Ecology C.F. Møllers Allé 3 8000 Aarhus C Fixed term full-time position 15 Feb 2027 - 14 Feb 2031 ID: 171484 Apply Four-year Researcher position on Greenland marine ecosystems The Department of Ecoscience, Aarhus University, invites applications for a four-year scientist position on the biodiversity and coastal ecosystem status and trends along Greenland’s coast with a special focus on the use of eDNA for monitoring of marine macroalgae. The position is linked to multiple international projects, including the Greenland Ecosystem Monitoring Programme with an overarching theme of studying the impacts of climate change on coastal ecosystems in Greenland. The position requires active participation in developing and attracting funding for new projects including a special focus on developing and implementing eDNA tools for the ecological research and monitoring. This is a four–year position available from 15 February 2027. Job description The position focuses on the ecology of coastal marine ecosystems in Greenland and their responses to climate change, particularly warming and the ongoing loss of the cryosphere. You are expected to participate in annual field campaigns in Greenland and contribute to the analysis and interpretation of monitoring and experimental data from coastal Greenland ecosystems. A particular focus will be on developing and applying environmental DNA (eDNA) methods for characterising and quantifying marine biodiversity, with an emphasis on marine macroalgae. This includes establishing high-quality biodiversity baselines and improving our capacity to detect changes in species distributions and the arrival of new species. Your profile Applicants must hold a PhD in biology or a closely related field. Documented experience with Arctic marine vegetation and ecosystem ecology is considered an advantage, together with expertise in eDNA-based approaches, including metabarcoding, quantitative PCR-based methods such as digital PCR (dPCR), bioinformatics and biostatistics. Experience with marine fieldwork, DNA barcoding, experimental design and morphological species identification is also an advantage. The successful candidate is expected to have experience in developing research ideas and in contributing to research proposals and grant applications. A scientific diving certification is considered an advantage. Fluency in spoken and written English is required. In addition, the candidate should enjoy working collaboratively in an interdisciplinary and international research environment and be motivated to contribute actively to fieldwork, research development and scientific publication. Who we are The Department of Ecoscience (https://ecos.au.dk/en/) is organised under the Faculty of Technical Sciences. The department’s research areas cover most aspects of biology and ecology, spanning all biological levels from genetics, physiological processes, individuals, populations and species to entire ecosystems. Strategic and applied research account for a large part of the research activities at the Department of Ecoscience. Geographically, the department works from the tropics to the poles, but with greater focus on Danish conditions. The department has an obligation towards the Ministry of Environment and Food of Denmark and the authorities in Greenland as national advisors on environmental issues. The department’s research, consultancy and teaching are linked to strong and active research groups. What we offer The successful candidate is offered: Access to a well-developed research infrastructure Office space and shared equipment a research climate inviting lively, open and critical discussion within and across different fields of research a working environment with teamwork, close working relations, network activities among young scientists and social activities a workplace characterized by professionalism, equality and a healthy work-life balance Place of work and area of employment The place of work is the main University campus in Aarhus, C.F. Møllers Allé 3, 8000 Aarhus C. Contact information For further information, please contact Mikael Sejr ( [email protected] ) or Dorte Krause-Jensen ( [email protected] ). Application procedure Shortlisting is used. This means that after the deadline for applications – and with the assistance from the assessment committee chairman, and the assessment committee if necessary, – the head of department selects the candidates to be evaluated. The selection is made on the basis of an assessment of who of the candidates are most relevant considering the requirements of the advertisement. All applicants will be notified within 6 weeks whether or not their applications have been sent to an expert assessment committee for evaluation. The selected applicants will be informed about the composition of the committee and will receive his/her assessment. Formalities and salary range Technical Sciences refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities under the Danish Ministry of Science, Technology and Innovation . The application must be in English and include a curriculum vitae, degree certificate, a complete list of publications, a statement of future research plans and information about research activities, teaching portfolio and verified information on previous teaching experience (if any). Guidelines for applicants can be found here. Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities. Salary and terms as agreed between the Danish Ministry of Taxation and the Confederation of Professional Unions at basic salary steps 4-8. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Research activities will be evaluated in relation to actual research time. Thus, we encourage applicants to specify periods of leave without research activities, in order to be able to subtract these periods from the span of the scientific career during the evaluation of scientific productivity. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including relocation service and career counselling to expat partners. Read more here . Please find more information about entering and working in Denmark here . The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website. Questions about the position\n                            ? Mikael Kristian Sejr Professor, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Ecology +4530454314 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Nat-Tech Administrative Centre - Nat-Tech HR [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Wednesday 18 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
    "https://international.au.dk/about/profile/vacant-positions/job/assistant-professorship-in-anthropology-aarhus-university": {
      "title": "Assistant Professorship in Anthropology, Aarhus University",
      "description": "Assistant Professorship in Anthropology, Aarhus University - Vacancy at Aarhus University Aarhus University logo For students For PhDs For employees Departments and faculties AU Library Brightspace MYSTUDIES.AU.DK Common pages for PhD students phd.au.dk PhD-portals Employee portals Find the local staff portal for your department or division. Departments and faculties Education International admissions at AU Bachelor's degree programmes Master's degree programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Meet AU Ask about studies Chat with our students International student blog Fairs and events On-demand webinars AU in many languages How to apply Bachelor’s degree programmes Master’s degree programmes Exchange programmes Summer University PhD programmes Education Research Research units and facilities Departments and schools Research centres Research facilities Research support Find a researcher PhD studies PhD at AU PhD programmes Vacant PhD positions How to apply Career services Researcher positions Vacant positions Fellowship programme at AIAS Attractive working conditions How to apply Funding opportunities Junior Researcher services Junior Researcher Association Campus resources Career services Research Life in Denmark Danish way of living Cost of living Family and work-life balance The Danes Learning and teaching culture Your new city Aarhus and surroundings Things to do in Aarhus Getting around AU locations For students Prepare your arrival Student housing Student life Future and career For PhDs and researchers Before arrival On arrival Housing Relocation and onboarding services Life in Denmark Collaboration How to collaborate with AU Business Collaboration Innovation and entrepreneurship Partner universities International alliances Technology Transfer at AU Commercialisation Technologies for licensing Spinouts Collaboration About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU Rankings Key statistics Strategy History Organisation Faculties Departments and schools Research centres Management Contact AU contact information and map AU locations Employee contact information International services Vacant positions Vacant positions Vacant PhD positions About AU You are here: AU About AU Profile Vacant positions About AU Profile Top reasons to choose AU AU in the world rankings Vacant positions Rules and Regulations Key statistics and annual reports Strategy Sustainability A changing campus History Alumni Honorary awards and grants Organisation AU for visitors Contact School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology - Faculty: Arts Assistant Professorship in Anthropology, Aarhus University Deadline 19 Nov 23:59 CET Expected start 1 Feb School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology Moesgård Allé 20 8270 Højbjerg Fixed term full-time position 1 Feb 2027 - 31 Jan 2030 ID: 171582 Apply The Department of Anthropology, School of Culture and Society, invites applications for a three-year position as assistant professor in relation to the research project “ Stories from my new life: Mobile transitions and social becomings among resettled refugees in Denmark” (TRANSIT). An assistant professorship is a full-time, three-year training position that involves research and teaching at the BA and MA level and includes an obligatory course in university teaching for assistant professors. The position will commence on 1 February, 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Place of employment: Department of Anthropology, Moesgaard Allé 20, 8270 Højbjerg, Denmark. The Faculty of Arts is committed to creating an inclusive working environment and therefore encourages all qualified candidates to apply, regardless of personal background, gender, sexual orientation, age, disability, ethnicity etc. The position The position will be associated with the research project TRANSIT at the Department of Anthropology and is a combined teaching and research position. Here is a brief description of the TRANSIT project: In 2021-2024 app. 600 Congolese women and children were resettled in Denmark under the UNHCR resettlement program. TRANSIT is concerned with resettled refugees’ life transitions, understood as a set of complex legal, social and existential transitions that are particularly urgent in the context of resettlement: 1) the transition from youth to adulthood; 2) the transition from being single to being married; and 3) the transition into old age and, ultimately, death. The project aims to establish a collaboration between Aarhus University, VIVE – The Danish Center for Social Science Research , FLUGT – Refugee Museum of Denmark, DFUNK – Dansk Flygtningehjælp Ungdom and a large group of resettled families in order to: a) create a mobile pop-up exhibition to be presented across Denmark in 2029; b) develop research-based teaching materials for pupils in the final years of Folkeskolen and in Gymnasiet on what it means to be resettled and start a new life in Denmark; and c) publish articles in leading peer-reviewed journals – based on a range of qualitative and quantitative data – on storytelling and life transitions following resettlement. The selected candidate is expected to do individual fieldwork, be main responsible for a work-package (developing research-based teaching material with FLUGT – Refugee Museum of Denmark), and to be a dedicated member of the project team and engaged in all the project activities and responsibilities. The position is offered with a view to attracting qualified applicants with an established and well - documented research record in innovative and internationally recognized research within anthropology and a specialization in migration and refugee studies, collaborative methods and creative forms of research dissemination. Research The selected applicant will be expected to contribute to core activities at the School of Culture and Society and Aarhus University in general and contribute to the Department of Anthropology’s research activities and output in particular. They will be expected to take an interest in interdisciplinary research collaboration within the Department of Anthropology, the School of Culture and Society, the Faculty of Arts, and beyond. The selected applicant will also be expected to develop new research projects with internal and external partners and to raise external research funding. The applicant’s research credentials and publication record within the field, e.g. anthropology, migration and refugee studies, collaborative methods and creative forms of research dissemination , will be assessed not just on existing publications and other research contributions but also on research potential. Past research output will be assessed based on the active research time of the applicant in question. We therefore ask applicants to specify any career breaks they have had (for instance due to maternity/paternity leave or sick leave) so we may discount these periods when assessing research productivity. Teaching The position will involve some teaching (up to 33% of the time) as agreed upon with the Head of the Department and the project PI. The selected applicant will be required to teach and supervise at BA and MA levels of the department’s degree programs in Anthropology and Human Security and will be expected to have teaching experience at university level. We emphasise the importance of maintaining a professional and respectful relationship between staff and students, so applicants should be able to demonstrate and exemplify their commitment to participatory teaching initiatives and student involvement as part of their teaching portfolio. Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD or equivalent qualifications in anthropology or a related discipline . They must also be able to document the following: An internationally oriented research profile documented through relevant academic publications, and possibly other research contributions, at the international level Experience of university-level teaching and a commitment to teaching development and the supervision of student projects Experience of or interest in active participation in international research collaboration Experience of or interest in obtaining external research funding Experience of or interest in research dessimination for a non-academic audience Applicants are asked to submit: A concise statement of motivation for applying for the position, including a description of experience with public research dessimination (maximum two pages). A full CV (one page). A full publication list (research outputs and public dissemination) A maximum of two publications. Only submitted publications will be assessed; a list of publications is not sufficient. As a result, applications without submitted publications will not be assessed. References or recommendations should not be included with the application. Applicants who are selected for a job interview may be asked to provide professional references. Language and further information Applicants can teach and supervise in English at university level. If the selected applicant is not fluent in Danish, they will be expected to acquire the language within a period of approximately two years. To maintain and develop the department’s research environment, the person appointed is expected to be present at the department on a regular basis. Applications must be uploaded in English. For further information about the TRANSIT project (including the project description), please contact, PI, Professor Mikkel Rytter, [email protected] For further information about the application procedure, please contact Human Resources: [email protected] . Knowledge exchange It is expected that the selected applicant will engage in knowledge exchange as described in the strategy for the Faculty of Arts Strategy Arts 2020-2025 (au.dk) , for instance research cooperation with private companies, government consultancy, cooperation with civil society partners or the public dissemination of knowledge. Applicants should document any prior experience within the field of knowledge exchange. School of Culture and Society The School of Culture and Society is a vibrant research community engaged in understanding the cultural and social conditions that shape human life. Our work examines how people interact with their environments, from prehistory to the present and across both local and global contexts. Through cross-sector and cross-disciplinary partnerships, we aim to support research innovation and contribute to addressing the major questions facing society. In both research and education, we are committed to bringing the humanities into active dialogue with partners beyond the university. The School is committed to: Promoting an international environment characterized by active academic and interdisciplinary collaboration. Encouraging innovative and experimental approaches to research, teaching, and communication. Cultivating environments that generate new knowledge and educate students for the future. Advancing broad engagement with digital humanities. Upholding a deep commitment to addressing both local and global societal challenges. Creating an inclusive, diverse, and sustainable workplace and organization. Read more about the school here School of Culture and Society - Aarhus University International applicants International applicants are encouraged to check Family and work-life balance in Denmark (au.dk) and Attractive working conditions (au.dk) for further information about the benefits of working at Aarhus University and in Denmark, including healthcare, paid holidays and, if relevant, maternity/paternity leave, childcare and schooling. Aarhus University offers a broad variety of services for international researchers and accompanying families, including a Relocation and onboarding services for international AU staff and career counselling for expat partners. For information about taxation, see Taxation aspects of international researchers’ employment by AU . Qualification requirements Applicants should hold a PhD or equivalent academic qualifications. Formalities Faculty of Arts refers to the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of Academic Staff at Danish Universities (the Appointment Order) . Further information on qualification requirements and job content may be found in the Memorandum on Job Structure for Academic Staff at Danish Universities . Further information on the application and supplementary materials may be found in Application Guidelines . The application must outline the applicant's motivation for applying for the position, attaching a curriculum vitae, a teaching portfolio, a complete list of published works, a research plan, copies of degree certificates and examples of academic production ( mandatory, but no more than two examples ). Please upload this material electronically along with your application. Please note that although the application process can be completed in the Aarhus University system without up-loading publications or a teaching portfolio, applications that do not include uploaded publications as well as a teaching portfolio (or equivalent documentation of teaching experience and qualifications) will not be considered. If nothing else is noted, applications must be submitted in English. Application deadline is at 11.59 pm Danish time (same as Central European Time) on the deadline day. Aarhus University’s ambition is to be an attractive and inspiring workplace for all and to foster a culture in which each individual has opportunities to thrive, achieve and develop. We view equality and diversity as assets, and we welcome all applicants. Shortlists may be prepared with the candidates that have been selected for a detailed academic assessment. A committee set up by the head of school is responsible for selecting the most qualified candidates. See this link for further information about shortlisting at the Faculty of Arts: shortlisting Terms of employment Appointment shall be in accordance with the collective labour agreement between the Danish Ministry of Finance and the Danish Confederation of Professional Associations. Salary and terms of employment are governed by the Cirkulære om overenskomst for akademikere i staten (in Danish). You will be employed as Assistant Professorship at base pay level 4–8 with additional supplements in accordance with the Cirkulære om protokollat om visse ansættelsesvilkår for videnskabeligt personale ved universiteter (in Danish). The job content and qualification requirements are described in further detail in the Ministerial Order on the Appointment of  Academic Staff at Universities . About Arts The Faculty of Arts is one of Northern Europe’s most significant faculties for research and higher education in the humanities, theology and education. Within this broad academic scope, the faculty comprises approximately 700 researchers, 200 PhD students, 9,000 Bachelor’s and Master’s degree students, and 1,500 further and continuing education students. We believe that the best ideas arise when different perspectives meet – and that research, teaching and innovation are best developed in dialogue with the surrounding society. You can find more information here: Faculty of Arts | Aarhus University The application must be submitted via Aarhus University’s recruitment system, which can be accessed under the job advertisement on Aarhus University's website . Questions about the position\n                            ? Mikkel Rytter Professor, School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology +4525149892 [email protected] Questions about application and proces\n                            ? Arts Administrative Centre - Arts HR +4523382165 [email protected] Apply Deadline: \n                            Thursday 19 Nov 2026 at 23:59 CET 37,500 students including PhD students 9,000 employees full-time equivalents 1,2 EUR billion in revenue Working at AU Key information for potential and future international employees AIAS-Fellowships See deadline and call for applications for programmes at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies (AIAS) PhD positions at Aarhus University See a full list of vacant PhD positions at Aarhus University How to apply for academic positions Revised\n    30.06.2026 - AU HR Aarhus University Nordre Ringgade 1 8000 Aarhus E-mail: [email protected] Tel: +45 8715 0000 CVR no: 31119103 EORI no: DK-31119103 About us Profile Departments and faculties Contact & map Vacant positions Degree programmes Bachelor's programmes Master’s programmes Engineering programmes Exchange programmes AU Summer University PhD programmes Shortcuts Library For students For PhDs For employees For Alumni © — Cookies at au.dk Privacy Policy Accessibility Statement 96261 / i48"
    },
